Suno’s approach to managing the fast-rising level of AI songs on the internet also includes using “new watermarking and fingerprinting techniques,” as stated in the blog post, which Shulman said are set to arrive “in the coming weeks…so we can partner even more closely with distribution platforms on combating fraud and misuse.&#8221;

Read the full blog post below:

How We&#8217;re Building the Future of Music Responsibly

By Mikey Shulman&nbsp;

We believe the future of music will be more participatory than ever before.&nbsp;

Music is one of the oldest and most universal forms of human expression, and it has always evolved alongside technology. The last wave of technology made it easier for people to find and listen to music. We believe this next wave will make it possible for far more people to experience the joys of creating it.

Our mission is to build the world’s best platform for music creation while contributing to a healthy and growing music ecosystem.&nbsp;

We&#8217;ve always believed that how we build matters just as much as what we build. From the beginning, we’ve held ourselves to a clear set of principles that help us make decisions in a fast-changing environment, always rooted in supporting artistry and creativity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Today we’re sharing those principles, how they already show up in our work, and the new actions we’re taking because of them.&nbsp;

Our Principles

Great Music is Made by People

Technology can unlock new ways to create, but it can’t replace the human experiences, emotions, and imperfections that make music meaningful.

That’s why we build our models and products alongside artists, songwriters, musicians, and producers. Every week, we host writing camps with artists at all stages of their careers to understand how our tools fit into their creative workflows, where they fall short, and what we should improve.&nbsp;

Our goal is to get inside the creative process with artists of varying backgrounds and approaches so we can build tools that support how they actually want to create.&nbsp;

Technology Opens New Possibilities for Creatives

We believe our tools should open new ways for artists to create, reach fans and build their careers. That belief is central to the next generation of music models we’re developing in partnership with the music industry.&nbsp;

As we build toward that future, we support artists today through several initiatives. We invest in educational programs that provide creative creators with resources to grow their careers. Through Spark , our creative funding and incubator program for emerging, unsigned artists, we provide grants, mentorship, and dedicated marketing support. And we’re exploring a range of mechanisms for artists to capture new opportunities and benefits that couldn’t have existed before this technology.

